WEBVTT

1
00:00:36.208 --> 00:00:43.791
<b>In the previous verse, Arjuna was confused </b>
<b>whether to renounce action or engage in it.</b>

2
00:00:43.791 --> 00:00:48.625
<b>In this verse, Lord Krishna is dispelling </b>
<b>this very dilemma of Arjuna.</b>

3
00:00:48.625 --> 00:00:50.083
<b>Lord Krishna says</b>

4
00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:55.833
<b>that both the paths of knowledge and </b>
<b>action lead a person towards liberation.</b>

5
00:00:55.833 --> 00:00:56.708
<b>But</b>

6
00:00:56.708 --> 00:01:00.458
<b>distinguishing between the two,</b>
<b>Lord Krishna states</b>

7
00:01:00.458 --> 00:01:06.041
<b>that the path of Karma Yoga is superior </b>
<b>to the path of Jnana Yoga.</b>

8
00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:16.541
<b>When both Jnana Yoga and Karma</b>
<b>Yoga lead to liberation,</b>

9
00:01:16.541 --> 00:01:20.208
<b>then why did Lord Krishna </b>
<b>call Karma Yoga better?</b>

10
00:01:20.208 --> 00:01:26.416
<b>In any action, the main thing is </b>
<b>the purpose behind it, the sentiment behind it.</b>

11
00:01:26.416 --> 00:01:27.500
<b>Suppose</b>

12
00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:32.625
<b>someone has chosen the path of renunciation,</b>
<b>turning away from worldly actions,</b>

13
00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:36.541
<b>but in doing so, what if their </b>
<b>mind hasn't been purified?</b>

14
00:01:36.541 --> 00:01:41.916
<b>If the attachments of the </b>
<b>world keep tormenting this person,</b>

15
00:01:41.916 --> 00:01:45.041
<b>can it be called renunciation?</b>

16
00:01:45.041 --> 00:01:51.916
<b>Renunciation isn't possible until the mind is </b>
<b>completely free from worldly sentiments.</b>

17
00:01:51.916 --> 00:01:55.708
<b>If desires and wishes remain unfulfilled,</b>

18
00:01:55.708 --> 00:01:59.791
<b>there's a possibility of getting caught in their attachments.</b>

19
00:01:59.791 --> 00:02:04.708
<b>On the path of Karma Yoga, there's no</b>
<b>attachment to the fruits of actions</b>

20
00:02:04.708 --> 00:02:07.208
<b>because there's a sense of faith in the mind.</b>

21
00:02:07.208 --> 00:02:10.166
<b>When action is considered a duty,</b>

22
00:02:10.166 --> 00:02:15.958
<b>both worldly actions and</b>
<b>spiritual purification are possible.</b>

23
00:02:15.958 --> 00:02:19.583
<b>In Karma Yoga, a person can choose actions</b>

24
00:02:19.583 --> 00:02:23.833
<b>that can aid in their spiritual enrichment.</b>

25
00:02:23.833 --> 00:02:29.541
<b>For this reason, Krishna, considering Karma Yoga</b>
<b>practical and accessible,</b>

26
00:02:29.541 --> 00:02:33.166
<b>is stating this path to be </b>
<b>better than renunciation.</b>

27
00:02:38.166 --> 00:02:42.208
<b>Whether it's renunciation or Karma Yoga,</b>

28
00:02:42.208 --> 00:02:46.375
<b>both lead to liberation,</b>

29
00:02:46.375 --> 00:02:47.375
<b>but</b>

30
00:02:47.375 --> 00:02:52.625
<b>Karma Yoga seems more </b>
<b>accessible and practical to me.</b>

31
00:02:52.625 --> 00:02:54.000
<b>What about you?</b>

32
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:59.791
<b>Life will bring many stages where, like Arjuna,</b>

33
00:02:59.791 --> 00:03:03.791
<b>numerous paths will be before you.</b>

34
00:03:03.791 --> 00:03:10.041
<b>Each path, with its unique potential, </b>
<b>will pull you towards it.</b>

35
00:03:10.041 --> 00:03:11.541
<b>So,</b>

36
00:03:11.541 --> 00:03:19.541
<b>which path will you choose? And on </b>
<b>what basis will you make this choice?</b>

37
00:03:19.541 --> 00:03:26.000
<b>Will you decide based on what others are doing, </b>
<b>based on the paths chosen by others?</b>

38
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:34.541
<b>If everyone is choosing a particular path, </b>
<b>it must be the best for me too.</b>

39
00:03:34.541 --> 00:03:38.666
<b>Do you think like that?</b>

40
00:03:38.666 --> 00:03:42.041
<b>Is such thinking even appropriate?</b>

41
00:03:42.041 --> 00:03:48.041
<b>What seems best to me is </b>
<b>what I've told Arjuna, but </b>

42
00:03:48.041 --> 00:03:56.291
<b>Arjuna will have to make the choice based </b>
<b>on his own logic, intellect, wisdom, and truth.</b>

43
00:03:56.291 --> 00:03:59.791
<b>In this world, every person is unique,</b>

44
00:03:59.791 --> 00:04:04.875
<b>with their special circumstances, </b>
<b>state of mind, and actions.</b>

45
00:04:04.875 --> 00:04:07.000
<b>You too.</b>

46
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:14.125
<b>So how can your path be </b>
<b>chosen based on someone else?</b>

47
00:04:14.125 --> 00:04:21.583
<b>If a tree is planted somewhere</b>
<b>other than its appropriate place,</b>

48
00:04:21.583 --> 00:04:25.416
<b> suppose it even takes root,</b>

49
00:04:25.416 --> 00:04:33.500
<b>but in the absence of its desired soil </b>
<b>and climate, will that tree be able to grow?</b>

50
00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:37.500
<b>Who knows you better than you?</b>

51
00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.583
<b>So how can the right to decide</b>

52
00:04:39.583 --> 00:04:49.416
<b>what's appropriate for you be given to </b>
<b>someone else or some pre-existing belief?</b>

53
00:04:49.416 --> 00:04:53.375
<b>Assess your situation with sincerity,</b>

54
00:04:53.375 --> 00:04:55.291
<b>probe your mind,</b>

55
00:04:55.291 --> 00:04:59.375
<b>identify your purpose with the use of wisdom,</b>

56
00:04:59.375 --> 00:05:03.833
<b>choose your path with this awakened behavior.</b>

57
00:05:03.833 --> 00:05:08.291
<b>This awareness itself is indicative of progress.</b>

58
00:05:08.291 --> 00:05:10.166
<b>It's not necessary</b>

59
00:05:10.166 --> 00:05:16.333
<b>that a path that seems attractive </b>
<b>will take you to your destination,</b>

60
00:05:16.333 --> 00:05:18.958
<b>but recognizing your dharma,</b>

61
00:05:18.958 --> 00:05:25.166
<b>you will certainly advance on </b>
<b>the path chosen by your wisdom.</b>

62
00:05:25.166 --> 00:05:30.625
<b>When you walk on your </b>
<b>chosen path with self-confidence,</b>

63
00:05:30.625 --> 00:05:33.666
<b>you'll also experience a wonderful peace.</b>

64
00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:43.708
<b>Your personal decisions may be limited to you.</b>

65
00:05:43.708 --> 00:05:45.333
<b>But</b>

66
00:05:45.333 --> 00:05:52.791
<b>every decision made in a family </b>
<b>or social context affects all those</b>

67
00:05:52.791 --> 00:05:56.375
<b>who are tied by the string </b>
<b>of familial relationships.</b>

68
00:05:56.375 --> 00:05:59.166
<b>Does it happen with you too</b>

69
00:05:59.166 --> 00:06:06.208
<b>that while making decisions, you find </b>
<b>yourself bound by established social practices?</b>

70
00:06:06.208 --> 00:06:12.000
<b>Just as everyone is doing, you </b>
<b>too are compelled to do the same,</b>

71
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:16.250
<b>and for this reason, you're unable</b>
<b>to make the right decision?</b>

72
00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:18.041
<b>To understand with an example,</b>

73
00:06:18.041 --> 00:06:23.000
<b>when you have to choose a </b>
<b>school for children's education,</b>

74
00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:28.708
<b>aren't you influenced by</b>
<b> relatives and colleagues?</b>

75
00:06:28.708 --> 00:06:35.000
<b>Don't you have to choose a particular </b>
<b>school for the sake of your social prestige?</b>

76
00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:38.708
<b>Such thinking is entirely inappropriate.</b>

77
00:06:38.708 --> 00:06:42.416
<b>By choosing someone else's attractive path,</b>

78
00:06:42.416 --> 00:06:44.791
<b>whose destination will you reach –</b>

79
00:06:44.791 --> 00:06:46.666
<b>yours</b>

80
00:06:46.666 --> 00:06:48.958
<b>or someone else's?</b>

81
00:06:48.958 --> 00:06:53.000
<b>By understanding your needs </b>
<b> and those of your family members,</b>

82
00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:56.875
<b>if you assess your real situation,</b>

83
00:06:56.875 --> 00:07:01.500
<b>if you choose your path with the use of wisdom,</b>

84
00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:07.666
<b>you will certainly be able to move </b>
<b>forward filled with self-confidence.</b>

85
00:07:12.666 --> 00:07:21.500
<b>Arjuna is in this dilemma of </b>
<b>whether to act or to renounce it.</b>

86
00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:27.958
<b>You must be facing such </b>
<b> dilemmas in your business too.</b>

87
00:07:27.958 --> 00:07:33.083
<b>Obstacles, challenges, and </b>
<b>dilemmas are the very steps</b>

88
00:07:33.083 --> 00:07:37.833
<b>on which you climb to </b>
<b>move forward in any business.</b>

89
00:07:37.833 --> 00:07:39.708
<b>The question is,</b>

90
00:07:39.708 --> 00:07:44.375
<b>what do you do when such a dilemma arises?</b>

91
00:07:44.375 --> 00:07:47.666
<b>What is your reaction? – </b>

92
00:07:47.666 --> 00:07:50.416
<b>run away leaving everything,</b>

93
00:07:50.416 --> 00:07:54.458
<b>or face that challenge head-on?</b>

94
00:07:54.458 --> 00:07:56.583
<b>Ok tell me one thing,</b>

95
00:07:56.583 --> 00:08:02.000
<b>Do you know of any player, artist, or entrepreneur</b>

96
00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:07.041
<b>who never had to face failure?</b>

97
00:08:07.041 --> 00:08:10.250
<b>Is it even possible?</b>

98
00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:17.000
<b>After starting any new work, </b>
<b>obstacles are bound to come;</b>

99
00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:23.666
<b>there will be so many hurdles that </b>
<b>you may not have even thought about.</b>

100
00:08:23.666 --> 00:08:31.583
<b>So what's the point of being surprised, scared, </b>
<b>or nervous about such hurdles?</b>

101
00:08:31.583 --> 00:08:35.333
<b>You may have been afraid of failure.</b>

102
00:08:35.333 --> 00:08:36.583
<b>But</b>

103
00:08:36.583 --> 00:08:43.166
<b>failure is an experience that</b>
<b>has a wonderful ability to teach.</b>

104
00:08:43.166 --> 00:08:46.291
<b>Think of it as a map –</b>

105
00:08:46.291 --> 00:08:51.375
<b>you are on this side, obstacles </b>
<b>and challenges in the middle,</b>

106
00:08:51.375 --> 00:08:54.583
<b>your goal on the other side.</b>

107
00:08:54.583 --> 00:08:56.583
<b>The one who leaves his responsibility,</b>

108
00:08:56.583 --> 00:08:59.833
<b>out of fear, turns his face the other way,</b>

109
00:08:59.833 --> 00:09:03.375
<b>who knows where he will reach.</b>

110
00:09:03.375 --> 00:09:04.666
<b>But</b>

111
00:09:04.666 --> 00:09:11.416
<b>if you stand firm in the face of challenges, </b>
<b>without fear, even in the toughest of tasks,</b>

112
00:09:11.416 --> 00:09:18.166
<b>even if you don't reach your goal,</b>
<b>you will certainly learn a lot.</b>

113
00:09:18.166 --> 00:09:25.000
<b>And then this failure will also give you </b>
<b>the experience to fight the next challenge.</b>

114
00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.083
<b>Remember,</b>

115
00:09:27.083 --> 00:09:29.666
<b>it is these experiences of life</b>

116
00:09:29.666 --> 00:09:36.625
<b>that in the future, improve our </b>
<b>self-confidence and prove helpful in success.</b>

